# Allowlist, not a denylist.
#
# Two reasons it is inverted. First, `.env` sits at the repo root and holds MODEL_API_KEY; a
# denylist that forgets one line pushes a credential into a public registry layer. Second, the
# build context is otherwise ~470 MB (.venv 422 M, units/ 44 M, f1_pipeline/data/ 14 M) and every
# byte of it is pull time charged against the unit clock.
#
# `f1_pipeline` needs three lines, not one: `!f1_pipeline` lets Docker traverse into the directory
# at all (a bare `*` above stops it there), `f1_pipeline/*` re-excludes everything inside it
# (the notebooks, README, and the 14 MB `data/` of backtest output), then `!f1_pipeline/m2_unit.py`
# allows back in the one file the image actually runs -- it reads nothing from `data/` at runtime,
# only the unit's own panel under `/input`.
*
!forecast_agent.py
!text_signal.py
!f1_pipeline
f1_pipeline/*
!f1_pipeline/m2_unit.py
